{"schema_version":"1.0","language":"en","edition":"en-ak","revision":"0","book":{"position":22,"code":"SNG","name":"Song of Songs","testament":"OT"},"chapter":6,"content":[{"type":"para","marker":"p","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"1","sid":"SNG 6:1"},"Whither is thy beloved gone, O thou fairest among women? whither is thy beloved turned aside? that we may seek him with thee. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 6:1"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"2","sid":"SNG 6:2"},"My beloved is gone down into his garden, to the beds of spices, to feed in the gardens, and to gather lilies. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 6:2"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"3","sid":"SNG 6:3"},"I ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["am"]}," my beloved’s, and my beloved ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," mine: he feedeth among the lilies. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 6:3"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"p","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"4","sid":"SNG 6:4"},"Thou ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["art"]}," beautiful, O my love, as Tirzah, comely as Jerusalem, terrible as ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["an army"]}," with banners. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 6:4"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"5","sid":"SNG 6:5"},"Turn away thine eyes from me, for they have overcome me: thy hair ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," as a flock of goats that appear from Gilead. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 6:5"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"6","sid":"SNG 6:6"},"Thy teeth ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are"]}," as a flock of sheep which go up from the washing, whereof every one beareth twins, and ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["there is"]}," not one barren among them. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 6:6"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"7","sid":"SNG 6:7"},"As a piece of a pomegranate ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are"]}," thy temples within thy locks. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 6:7"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"8","sid":"SNG 6:8"},"There are threescore queens, and fourscore concubines, and virgins without number. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 6:8"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"9","sid":"SNG 6:9"},"My dove, my undefiled is ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["but"]}," one; she ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," the ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["only"]}," one of her mother, she ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," the choice ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["one "]},"of her that bare her. The daughters saw her, and blessed her; ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["yea,"]}," the queens and the concubines, and they praised her. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 6:9"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"p","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"10","sid":"SNG 6:10"},"Who ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," she ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["that"]}," looketh forth as the morning, fair as the moon, clear as the sun, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and"]}," terrible as ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["an army "]},"with banners? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 6:10"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"11","sid":"SNG 6:11"},"I went down into the garden of nuts to see the fruits of the valley, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and"]}," to see whether the vine flourished, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and"]}," the pomegranates budded. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 6:11"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"12","sid":"SNG 6:12"},"Or ever I was aware, my soul made me ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["like"]}," the chariots of Amminadib. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 6:12"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"13","sid":"SNG 6:13"},"Return, return, O Shulamite; return, return, that we may look upon thee. What will ye see in the Shulamite? As it were the company of two armies. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 6:13"}]}]}
